  "description": "One of airBaltic's three Baltic flag A220-300s, for Estonia: the fin in the flag's level bands (blue over black over white), and the fuselage wrapped in waves of the same colors, a blue band through the window line and a black one under it, rolling from the nose (black at its tip) to the tail, with white above and a white belly ahead of the black's sweep down behind the wing; the tail cone blue over a black keel. Lime engines and winglets with dark 'airBaltic' as on the standard scheme, a small white 'airBaltic' on the black under the cockpit. No fuselage or fin title.",
