  "notes": "Left side only in open photos (2019-2021); the right side is taken to match (mirrored), as on the Latvian and Lithuanian flag jets. The fin's bands measured level at 0.315 and 0.665 of its height. The waves' edges were found column by column on the 2020 photo; under the wing and engine (x 0.38-0.55) they're joined smoothly between what shows either side: low confidence there. The registration with the EU and Latvian flags sits on the black aft of the wing (white); not drawn.",
  "history": "Applied in 2019 to YL-CSJ (in the standard scheme in December 2018), alongside a Latvian and a Lithuanian flag jet for the Baltic states' centenaries."
}
